<blockquote class="uncited"><div><blockquote class="uncited"><div><span style="text-decoration:underline"></span><strong class="text-strong"></strong>However, I know that in the file [<strong class="text-strong">operation.doc</strong>] it says:<br>Following two are for the version of 100,000 contacts<br>MD-9600(CSV-GPS)-P26.45.bin <span style="color:#FF0000">for GPS version</span><br>MD-9600(CSV)-V26.45.bin <span style="color:#FF0000">for common version</span><br><br>But I don't care about that. My problem is that <strong class="text-strong">the GPS doesn't change from the None option</strong>.<br>I'm trying to find a solution to this.<br>Maybe it's a faulty device.</div></blockquote>Operation.doc ? , where have you found that file ?<br>(Sounds like some factory document, that is not valid when you run OpenGD77) <br><br><a href="https://github.com/LibreDMR/OpenGD77_UserGuide/blob/master/OpenGD77_User_Guide.md#download-links-and-other-resources" class="postlink">https://github.com/LibreDMR/OpenGD77_Us ... -resources</a><br><blockquote class="uncited"><div>Donor File for TYT MD-9600 | Retevis RT-90 | TYT MD-UV380 | Retevis RT-3S | Baofeng DM-1701 | Retevis RT-84<br><a href="https://www.passion-radio.com/index.php?controller=attachment&amp;id_attachment=760" class="postlink">https://www.passion-radio.com/index.php ... chment=760</a><br>Unzip the donor firmware zip file, extract the donor file 'MD9600-CSV(2571V5)-V26.45.bin' and save it to your computer.<br>Note, this file is the same for all of the radio types above.</div></blockquote>OpenGD77 detects if there is any NMEA serial output activity when radio is started and if so it can be activated.</div></blockquote>Be careful. Inside the file [210525 MD-9600 V4 firmware for PLL2571.zip] there is [Operation.doc].<p>Statistics: Posted by <a href="http://localhost/opengd77/memberlist.php?mode=viewprofile&amp;u=7586">SV2BBO</a> — Sun Feb 02, 2025 6:54 am</p><hr />
]]></content>
