<blockquote class="uncited"><div><span style="text-decoration:underline"></span><strong class="text-strong"></strong>However, I know that in the file [<strong class="text-strong">operation.doc</strong>] it says:<br>Following two are for the version of 100,000 contacts<br>MD-9600(CSV-GPS)-P26.45.bin <span style="color:#FF0000">for GPS version</span><br>MD-9600(CSV)-V26.45.bin <span style="color:#FF0000">for common version</span><br><br>But I don't care about that. My problem is that <strong class="text-strong">the GPS doesn't change from the None option</strong>.<br>I'm trying to find a solution to this.<br>Maybe it's a faulty device.</div></blockquote>Hence, no GPS is fitted, or it's faulty. This is why you can't enable it.<br>The firmware turns the GPS module on at boot time, after installation, and looks for NMEA sentences, <strong class="text-strong">and this on every platforms</strong>, except the GD-77S and RD-5R.<p>Statistics: Posted by <a href="http://localhost/opengd77/memberlist.php?mode=viewprofile&amp;u=56">F1RMB</a> — Sun Feb 02, 2025 6:27 am</p><hr />
]]></content>
