<strong class="text-strong"><strong class="text-strong"></strong></strong><span style="text-decoration:underline"></span>I have the <strong class="text-strong">Retevis RT3S</strong> with <strong class="text-strong">GPS</strong>. S/N: 2308R03S1104481 APR.2024.<br>In Firmware loader if I select either [MD9600-CSV-GPS(2571V5)-P26.45.bin] or [MD9600-GPS-REC(2571V5)-S26.45.bin] donor file, this message appears:<br><em class="text-italics">"The file you selected was NOT the official firmware version MD9600-CSV(2571V5)-V26.45.bin"</em><br>But in [operation.doc] it says:<br>Following two are for the version of 100.000 contacts<br>MD-9600(CSV-GPS)-P26.45.bin for GPS version <br>MD-9600(CSV)-V26.45.bin for common version <br>I am forced to continue with <strong class="text-strong">MD9600-CSV(2571V5)-V26.45.bin</strong> and [<strong class="text-strong">OpenMDUV380.zip</strong>] firmware.<br>The Firmware loader completes normally but in General Options the <strong class="text-strong">GPS </strong>is set to <strong class="text-strong"><span style="color:#FF0000">None </span></strong>and <strong class="text-strong"><span style="color:#FF0000">does not change</span></strong> when the [Select] knob is turned.<br>I have tried both the stable [R20240908] and the Beta version 2025 01 28 of [OpenMDUV380.zip] Firmware.<br>Any idea what is going on?<p>Statistics: Posted by <a href="http://localhost/opengd77/memberlist.php?mode=viewprofile&amp;u=7586">SV2BBO</a> — Sat Feb 01, 2025 6:14 pm</p><hr />
]]></content>
